 father  Zara who was the first peasant to become  a magic knight  Sora's father had great respect for the  magic knight title and he did his very  best to serve honorably and to help  those in need  Sora's father loved being a magic night  and he ingrained this love and respect  for this noble position within zora as  well even though he failed to pass the  magic Knight exam many times Sora's  father kept on trying until he finally  became a knight he was an extremely  cheerful person who loved to joke around  and pull  friendly pranks on Sora and more than  anything Sora's father always told his  son how much he loves being a magic  knight how much he loves helping those  in need  and how much he loves fighting alongside  other powerful and honorable magic  knights in this sense austin reminds or  of his father and this is one of the  reasons why sore eventually warms up to  hasta  Sora greatly admired his father and his  current appearance is actually based on  a doll that his father made for him back  when he was 12 a doll which his father  had named the emissary of justice super  mage Sora  unfortunately Sora's father Zahra was  killed in battle he had been a member of  the purple orcas squad and one day when  he was visiting his father's grave Zhora  overheard some other members of the  purple orcas talking about how Zara was  actually betrayed by his own squad  members apparently many of the magic  Knights in his own squad looked down on  Zara for being a peasant and for caring  too much about helping other peasants  and it appears that one of his fellow  magic Knights attacked Zara from behind  Zhora is absolutely devastated after  hearing this and his entire life is  shattered when he gets older  Sora makes it his mission to stand up to  corrupt magic knights who mistreat  others especially peasants he uses his  impressive magical and physical  abilities to fearless Lee take on  high-ranking magic Knights and teach  them a lesson but despite the fact that  